# Same source subnet, same destination, same port. The only variable
# separating "allow" from "deny" is App-ID's classification of the
# session: some sessions never get past the provisional "ssl" guess
# before the client disconnects; most run long enough for Content-ID to
# see the actual (non-TLS) payload and reclassify as unknown-tcp, which
# is denied.

